{"kind": "journal", "text": "Findings: three independently robust families on this panel. 1) Intermediate momentum ret 60-120d, stronger with a 10-20d implementation gap (delay(ret(60),10) SR 1.12 standalone; corroborated by delay(ret(40),20), delay(ret(60),20), sub(ret(120),ret(10))). 2) Short 3d reversal, best expressed as neg(minr(3)) SR 1.00 and ma(3) SR 0.87. 3) High return kurtosis, kurt(60/120/250) all positive standalone, kurt(120) adds ~0.15-0.25 SR to every stack. Skew was lookback-inconsistent and diluted combos - dropped. Vol, beta, corr tilts hurt. Equal-weight cs_z sums of validated blocks form a flat plateau at train SR 1.45-1.70; differences among top variants are within noise, so final picks are three plateau members with varied block definitions and weights rather than the single argmax, to limit selection overfit. Stopping at 6 of 12 batches deliberately.", "ts": "2026-09-01T06:22:43.081398+00:00"}
{"kind": "report", "top3_chosen": ["add(add(add(cs_z(ret(120)), cs_z(delay(ret(60), 10))), add(cs_z(ma(3)), cs_z(neg(minr(3))))), cs_z(kurt(120)))", "add(add(cs_z(delay(ret(60), 10)), cs_z(neg(minr(3)))), cs_z(kurt(120)))", "add(add(add(cs_z(sub(ret(120), ret(10))), cs_z(delay(ret(60), 10))), add(cs_z(ma(3)), cs_z(neg(minr(3))))), cs_z(kurt(120)))"], "chosen_sr_train": [1.6767, 1.678, 1.6746], "rationale": "All three sit on a broad stable plateau (train SR 1.45-1.70 across ~25 variants) combining three independently validated families: intermediate momentum (ret 60-120d, strongest with a 10-20d gap, standalone SR 0.7-1.1), short-term 3d reversal (via price-to-3d-min and MA3-to-price, standalone SR 0.7-1.0), and high return kurtosis over 60-120d (standalone SR 0.4-0.7). Equal-weight cs_z sums of validated blocks were preferred over the single argmax expression to limit selection overfit, and the three picks vary block definitions and weights to hedge parameterization risk.", "n_batches_used": 6, "ts": "2026-09-01T06:22:49.095141+00:00"}
